  "codex_last_message": "Changed `src/db.rs` so `VDB_ENABLE_PQ_PRESCORE` actually activates the PQ path instead of silently falling back to default vector-radius pruning, and updated the ANN harness in `.meta_codex/tools/measure_ann_search_only`, `.meta_codex/tools/measure_ann_benchmark`, `.meta_codex/tools/sweep_ann_search_only`, and `.meta_codex/tools/sweep_ann_benchmark` to make that override explicit and sweepable. I also updated `.meta_codex/strategy.md`, `.meta_codex/research_notes.md`, `.meta_codex/campaign_journal.md`, and `.meta_codex/tools/README.md` to record the correction.\n\nThe main result is negative but important: the old cycle-40 \u201cPQ win\u201d was a false positive from the flat radius-pruned path. With real PQ enabled, `14 / 136 / 352` measured about `5981.98` local QPS but only `0.6920` recall, and a local PQ sweep up to `3072` prescore candidates still only reached about `0.9340` recall. A fresh exact fast `u8`-routing retry also regressed to `4521.59 QPS`, `0.9533` recall, so I left the default fallback untouched. `build_project` succeeded, default `run_correctness_test` still passed at `1.0000`, and current score expectations are unchanged: the scored official path is still roughly low-`10k` to low-`12k`, while the real ANN fallback is still only low-`5k` class on this host.\n\nNext best move: stop treating the old global-PQ numbers as evidence and build a stronger shortlist signal, most likely residual-aware or cluster-local PQ/codebooks, rather than spending another cycle on budget sweeps or stale routing toggles.",
